    "text": {
     "en": "Madhu loved food and wanted to eat many kinds of food and snacks. Every day at noon he sat under a banyan tree to eat his lunch.\nOne day an old man came. Madhu felt sorry for him and shared his food.\nThe old man was so happy that he told Madhu he could wish for anything from the tree.\nMadhu thought he would ask for different types of food forever. He said, Let me have different types of food, nothing else. The tree asked him to think it over, but he said Nothing else without thinking.\nFirst he asked for laddoos and other foods. The story shows what happens when we wish without thinking carefully.\nA wise wish thinks about family, friends and others too, not only ourselves.\nNew words: wish, banyan, granted."
    }
